ely 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 26%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $67K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $34K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Trupanion, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.5B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years and +26% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -26% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 17% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $75M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.60\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 16% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 153% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5289606426561364},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 28% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trupanion (TRUP) Stock Trades At A Premium To Its Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-trup/trupanion/news/trupanion-trup-stock-trades-at-a-premium-to-its-earnings","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794561990.864,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Trupanion (NASDAQ:TRUP) Price Target Raised to $33.00","source":"thelincol